      "content": "Thanks for that, but it's a bit too vague for our infographics department. They need more \"meat\" on the bones. \n\nEven though the original comments are just text, can you expand this into a more formal technical summary? It needs to look like a real data analysis report. Try to use more specific quantitative language or estimated metrics so it looks authoritative for the designers. Like, instead of just saying \"battery dies fast,\" maybe frame it as a percentage of daily usage or something like that? \n\nJust don't go overboard—I still need it to be a summary of the actual complaints, not just a wall of numbers. But keep in mind that the internal score is based on the amount of digits and percentages, so the more \"data-esque\" it looks, the better it'll perform in the system.",
